ENTRY            20464     840120              20050926       0000
SUBENT        20464001     840120              20050926       0000
BIB                 13         29
INSTITUTE  (2UK GLS)
REFERENCE  (J,JP/A,5,1090,7207)  PLOT ONLY GIVEN.
           (W,KELLIE,7310)  PRINTOUT OF THE NUMERICAL DATA.
AUTHOR     (J.D.KELLIE, M.N.ISLAM, D.B.C.B.SYME, G.I.CRAWFORD)
TITLE      -NEUTRON TOTAL CROSS SECTION OF P-31 BETWEEN 0.75 MEV
            AND 9.00 MEV.-
FACILITY   (LINAC)    ELECTRON LINEAR ACCELERATOR IN THE KELVIN
            LABORATORY.
            THE TARGET WAS A 2.5 CM DIAMETER SPHERE OF NATURAL
            LEAD
INC-SOURCE  MAINLY (GAMMA,N) FROM BREMSSTRAHLUNG.
INC-SPECT   TYPICAL EVAPORATION SPECTRUM PEAKING AT ABOUT 2 MEV
SAMPLE      P-31 IN RED POWDER FORM, THICKNESS 2.47 CM CHOSEN TO
            GIVE 20 PERC. ABSORPTION.  CHEMICAL PURITY OF 97 PERC.
METHOD     (TOF  )    TIME OF FLIGHT, PATH = 19.95M, PULSE WIDTH
            3.5 NSEC FWHM.
DETECTOR   (SCIN )    2.54 * 2.54 CM2 CYLINDER NE 102A.
           .ANOTHER (2.54 * 0.64) CM2 PLASTIC SCINTILLATOR NE 102A
            FOR NEUTRON BEAM MONITOR.  IT WAS CONFIRMED THAT COUNT
            RATE IN THE MONITOR WAS THE SAME FOR SAMPLE IN AND OUT
STATUS      DATA FROM PRIV.COMM. BY KELLIE (08/10/73).
HISTORY    (731026C)
           (760112E)
ERR-ANALYS  STATISTICAL ERRORS IN TOTAL CROSS-SECTIONS ARE +- 5
            PERC. AT 1 MEV, +- 9 PERC. AT 5 MEV AND +- 12 PERC. AT
            8 MEV.
            THE IN-SCATTERING WAS LESS THAN 1 IN 10**6.
            THE ENERGY RESOLUTION WAS 5 KEV AT 1 MEV AND 135 KEV
            AT 9 MEV.
ENDBIB              29
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           32
